      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-33666",
      ":question/problem": "Find the shortest distance between the origin and the osculating plane for the curve $r(t)$ at the point where $t=1,$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =6t\\,i+2{t}^{3}\\,j+3\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}\\,k \\\\ T(t) & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}(i+{t}^{2}\\,j+\\sqrt{2}tk) \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}(-\\sqrt{2}t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}t\\,j+(1-{t}^{2})k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively."
